---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="CV" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-4 mb-3">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">CV</h1>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/cv.pdf" download>Download CV (PDF)</a>
  </div>
  <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-1">
    AI Solutions Architect &middot; Generative AI, RAG &amp; Agentic Systems &middot; Enterprise AI Delivery
  </div>
  <div class="text-sm opacity-70 mb-10">
    Riyadh, Saudi Arabia &middot; <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/eidam/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">linkedin.com/in/eidam</a>
    &middot; <a href="mailto:ahmedmeid@gmx.com" class="link">ahmedmeid@gmx.com</a>
  </div>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Profile</h2>
    <p class="opacity-80 text-justify">
      AI Solutions Architect with 18+ years spanning enterprise, solution, cloud, and AI architecture, including
      hands-on production delivery of generative AI, RAG, and agentic systems for large-scale, regulated
      organizations. I'm currently embedded within the Saudi Public Investment Fund (PIF) as part of a dedicated AI
      solutions team, taking GenAI use cases from discovery and ideation through PoC and production on Palantir
      Foundry and AIP &mdash; personally building RAG pipelines with vector, hybrid, and graph-based retrieval,
      agentic workflows orchestrated with AIP Logic, chatbot applications, and recurring LLM evaluation and
      regression-testing suites, while leading and mentoring a data engineering team. This flagship engagement caps
      a multi-sector NEOM consulting portfolio spanning Food, Environment, Energy &amp; Water, Hotels, and the
      University of NEOM, across digital strategy, data strategy, business capability mapping, procurement, and
      system design. I'm skilled at translating ambiguous business problems into scalable, well-governed AI
      architectures while partnering with executive stakeholders. I recently completed an M.Sc. in Artificial
      Intelligence (University of Texas at Austin, GPA 3.93) and am certified across the full Google Cloud
      AI/data/platform stack, plus AWS Solutions Architect Professional and Palantir.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-5">Core Competencies</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Generative AI &amp; Agentic Systems</h3>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
          LLMs, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (vector, hybrid &amp; graph-based retrieval), agentic/autonomous
          workflows, prompt &amp; context engineering, Palantir AIP Logic orchestration, ASR pipelines.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">AI Engineering &amp; Evaluation</h3>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
          LLM evaluation datasets &amp; regression testing (retrieval relevance, groundedness, latency, cost),
          embeddings &amp; vector search, model explainability (Grad-CAM, SHAP), MLOps &amp; model monitoring, cost
          &amp; latency optimization.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">System Design &amp; Architecture</h3>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
          Enterprise &amp; Cloud Architecture, Reference Architectures, HLD/LLD, Integration &amp; Data-Flow Design,
          NFRs, Secure Landing Zones, Cost/Option Analyses.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Architecture Governance</h3>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
          Technical Evaluation &amp; Compliance Reviews, RFP Development, Vendor &amp; Solution Assessment, BDAT
          Domains (Business, Data, Application, Technology).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Platforms &amp; Cloud</h3>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
          Palantir Foundry &amp; AIP, Google Cloud (Vertex AI, BigQuery), AWS, Python/PyTorch/Hugging Face, Docker
          &amp; Kubernetes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Leadership &amp; Delivery</h3>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
          Engineering Team Leadership &amp; Mentoring, Digital &amp; Data Strategy, Executive Stakeholder Engagement,
          Procurement Advisory, PoC-to-Production Delivery.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-5">Experience</h2>
    <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4">
      <TimeLineElement title="AI & Cloud Solutions Architect &mdash; TONOMUS (NEOM)" subtitle="Riyadh, Saudi Arabia &middot; Oct 2021 &ndash; Present">
        <p class="text-left opacity-70 italic mb-2">
          Embedded solutions consultant serving multiple NEOM sector clients across the full engagement lifecycle
          &mdash; from digital &amp; data strategy through business capability mapping, procurement advisory, system
          design, and technology consulting &mdash; culminating in hands-on production AI delivery at PIF.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-left">
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">PIF flagship delivery:</span> architected and hands-on built an end-to-end
            enterprise GenAI system on Palantir Foundry &amp; AIP &mdash; RAG pipelines, ASR ingestion, agentic
            workflows, RBAC, lineage, and telemetry &mdash; designed to production-grade NFRs (security, latency,
            cost, observability) in a regulated public-sector environment.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Hands-on engineering ownership:</span> personally built and owned
            production Foundry components &mdash; data pipelines, ontology objects, chatbot applications, RAG
            pipelines, and data visualizations &mdash; with agentic orchestration implemented in AIP Logic.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Advanced retrieval:</span> designed and built enterprise RAG pipelines
            combining vector, hybrid, and graph-based retrieval &mdash; source curation, chunking, embeddings, and
            prompt orchestration &mdash; for grounded, source-attributed answers.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">LLM evaluation &amp; regression testing:</span> defined evaluation datasets
            and recurring regression tests covering retrieval relevance, groundedness, latency, and cost.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Engineering leadership:</span> led and mentored the data engineering team of
            Saudi fresh-graduate engineers through design reviews and delivery ownership.
          </li>
          <li>
            Authored NEOM enterprise AI and cloud reference architectures, landing zones, HLD/LLD, integration
            architectures, and NFR &amp; cost/option analyses across sector programs &mdash; Food, Environment,
            Energy &amp; Water, Hotels, and University of NEOM.
          </li>
          <li>
            Advised on procurement and technology selection, and facilitated AI discovery workshops and executive
            presentations for senior client stakeholders.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </TimeLineElement>

      <TimeLineElement title="Solution Architect &mdash; Mobily" subtitle="Riyadh, Saudi Arabia &middot; Jul 2017 &ndash; Sep 2021">
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-left">
          <li>
            Partnered with business and IT stakeholders to define, review, and refine requirements, ensuring
            alignment with architectural standards; led architecture presentations and workshops to walk through
            proposed solutions and gather governance feedback.
          </li>
          <li>
            Documented solution architecture artifacts &mdash; business use cases, data flows, functional/
            non-functional requirements &mdash; and produced system diagrams identifying interdependencies and
            risks, across IT, network, and security domains.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </TimeLineElement>

      <TimeLineElement title="Senior Consultant &mdash; Ericsson" subtitle="Sulaymaniyah, Iraq &middot; Jul 2013 &ndash; Jun 2017">
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-left">
          <li>
            Provided hands-on architecture support on a large-scale Telecom IT Transformation program for Asiacell
            Telecom, leading a development team customizing the BSCS iX R3 billing platform.
          </li>
          <li>
            Advised management on development estimates, technical risk, and architecture/technology choices; built
            integration endpoints between BSCS iX and CRBT, online mediation, POS, and CRM platforms.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </TimeLineElement>

      <TimeLineElement title="Consultant &mdash; Atos" subtitle="Rabat, Morocco &middot; Aug 2012 &ndash; Jun 2013">
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-left">
          <li>
            Designed and implemented software applications for new products and offers for Maroc Telecom, including
            a Spring Batch application for tariff-model changes and an end-to-end location-monitoring service.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </TimeLineElement>

      <TimeLineElement title="Software Engineer &mdash; Xpress Integration & Ericsson" subtitle="Cairo, Egypt &middot; Jul 2008 &ndash; Jul 2012">
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-left">
          <li>
            Designed and developed the SPT (Smart Promotion Tool) and a SQL query-builder module for
            customer-eligibility targeting, plus re-rating batch processing; earlier built GSM network-simulation
            and mass-service-activation tooling at Ericsson.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </TimeLineElement>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-5">Education</h2>
    <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4">
      <TimeLineElement
        title="M.Sc. in Artificial Intelligence &mdash; University of Texas at Austin"
        subtitle="Sep 2024 &ndash; May 2026 &middot; GPA 3.93/4.00"
      >
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-left">
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Selected project &mdash; Medical Imaging Diagnostic Pipeline:</span> trained
            a brain-cancer classification model with structured error analysis and Grad-CAM/SHAP explainability,
            reducing false positives by 13%.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Selected project &mdash; Vision-Language Model Fine-Tuning:</span> fine-tuned
            a VLM for visual question answering, covering preprocessing, augmentation, experiment tracking, and
            structured evaluation.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </TimeLineElement>

      <TimeLineElement
        title="Postgraduate Diploma in Software Engineering &mdash; ITI"
        subtitle="Cairo, Egypt &middot; Jul 2007 &ndash; Jun 2008"
      />

      <TimeLineElement
        title="B.Sc. in Mathematics and Computer Science &mdash; Menoufia University"
        subtitle="Shebin Elkom, Egypt &middot; Sep 2001 &ndash; May 2005"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-5">Certifications</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Google Cloud</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-sm opacity-80">
          <li>Professional Machine Learning Engineer</li>
          <li>Professional Data Engineer</li>
          <li>Professional Cloud Architect</li>
          <li>Generative AI Leader</li>
          <li>Associate Cloud Engineer</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">AWS</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-sm opacity-80">
          <li>Solutions Architect &ndash; Professional</li>
          <li>DevOps Engineer &ndash; Professional</li>
          <li>Solutions Architect &ndash; Associate</li>
          <li>Cloud Practitioner</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Palantir</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 space-y-1 text-sm opacity-80">
          <li>Foundry Data Engineer Associate</li>
          <li>Foundry Application Developer Associate</li>
          <li>Foundry &amp; AIP Builder</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-5">Languages</h2>
    <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-2">
      <li><span class="font-semibold">Arabic</span> <span class="opacity-70 text-sm">&mdash; Native</span></li>
      <li><span class="font-semibold">English</span> <span class="opacity-70 text-sm">&mdash; Fluent</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
